    {
      "id": "cover-flat-copy-and-barcode",
      "requirementId": "R-cover-flat-copy-and-barcode",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "cover-flat"
      ],
      "criteria": "On the flat, read the three panels separately. The front panel must carry both the title and the descriptor line. The spine panel must carry the imprint with its letters running so the words are read from the head down to the foot when the book stands upright; bottom-to-top or horizontally stacked letters fail. The back panel must hold a machine-style barcode block with the ISBN digits, placed in its lower right quadrant and clearly wider than tall in roughly a 40:25 ratio; a barcode centred, on the front, or square/portrait in proportion fails. Exact millimetre measurement is not expected — position and proportion are the evidence.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "per-artifact"
    },
    {
      "id": "caption-fields-order-and-record",
      "requirementId": "R-caption-fields-order-and-record",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "spread-plate-03",
        "spread-plate-10",
        "spread-plate-18"
      ],
      "criteria": "In each spread's caption block the four items must be readable in the stated sequence, top to bottom or left to right, with the credit last. The wording of the collection title, the accession number and the date-and-maker text must agree with the record for that plate (plate-03 = 46447i, plate-10 = 46168i, plate-18 = 46180i). Failure: a field missing, two fields swapped, an accession number belonging to a different plate, a shortened or paraphrased collection title, or a date or maker not in the record. Typographic styling of the fields (weight, italic, small caps, line breaks, separating rules) is free.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "per-artifact"
    },
    {
      "id": "absent-record-strings",
      "requirementId": "R-absent-record-strings",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "spread-plate-03",
        "spread-plate-10",
        "spread-plate-18"
      ],
      "criteria": "Where the record has no year or no maker, the caption must show the standing placeholder wording rather than an empty slot, a dash, 'unknown', 'n.d.', 'anon.' or a guessed date. The plate-03 caption needs the date placeholder and the maker names from the record; the plate-10 caption needs both placeholders; the plate-18 caption needs the maker placeholder and its bracketed place. Inventing a year or an engraver for any of these is a failure.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "per-artifact"
    },
    {
      "id": "credit-and-rights-close",
      "requirementId": "R-credit-and-rights-close",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "spread-plate-03",
        "spread-plate-10",
        "spread-plate-18"
      ],
      "criteria": "Each caption must end with the source name and the rights wording together, as the last of the four items. Either one alone, a different rights phrase (CC0, 'copyright free', 'public domain' in other words), or the credit floated away from the caption into a folio or margin is a failure. A separator between the two (dash, bullet, slash, new line) is allowed.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "per-artifact"
    },
    {
      "id": "grid-and-caption-zone",
      "requirementId": "R-grid-and-caption-zone",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "spread-plate-03",
        "spread-plate-10",
        "spread-plate-18",
        "opener-chapter-1",
        "index-by-accession"
      ],
      "criteria": "Compare the pages as a group. Plate images, headings, thumbnails and caption text must start and stop on a repeating vertical structure that reads as six equal columns with narrow gutters; elements may span several columns but must not cut a column in half differently on each page. The outer margin must read narrower than the foot margin, and those margins must be the same width on every page in the set. Every caption block must sit as a band at the bottom of the type area, occupying roughly the lowest eighth of it and never rising into the middle of the page or dropping below the foot margin. Failure: one page on a visibly different column count or margin set, or a caption floated beside or above the plate.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "set"
    },
    {
      "id": "chapter-one-opener-thumbnails",
      "requirementId": "R-chapter-one-opener-thumbnails",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "opener-chapter-1"
      ],
      "criteria": "The opener must name the chapter and show exactly nine distinct small reproductions, each recognisably one of the coloured constellation cards supplied for that chapter, with no card shown twice and none replaced by a plate from a later chapter. Ornamental or invented star drawings standing in for a card fail. Thumbnail size, arrangement and grid position are the designer's call as long as all nine read as the same family of reproductions.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "per-artifact"
    },
    {
      "id": "index-spread-accession-labels",
      "requirementId": "R-index-spread-accession-labels",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "index-by-accession"
      ],
      "criteria": "Count the thumbnails: ten, one per plate from the later four chapters, grouped under those four chapter headings with the right plates beneath each heading. Each thumbnail must carry a readable accession number, and those numbers must match the record for the plate shown. Failure: a missing or repeated plate, a plate filed under the wrong chapter, an unlabelled thumbnail, or a number that belongs to another plate. Chapter 1 cards may not appear here.",
      "inputFiles": [
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/scenarios/bench-da-book-base-a-n06.json",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/01-client-facts.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/02-delivery-catalog.en.md",
        "benchmarks/design-anything/v0.6/assets/bench-da-book-base-a-n06/03-plate-records.md"
      ],
      "visualScope": "per-artifact"
    },
    {
      "id": "primary-ink-throughout",
      "requirementId": "R-primary-ink-throughout",
      "method": "visual",
      "targetSlots": [
        "cover-flat",
        "opener-chapter-1",
        "spread-plate-03",
        "spread-plate-10",
        "spread-plate-18",
        "index-by-accession"
      ],
      "criteria": "Across the delivered pages, the designer's own ink — rules, headings, folios, caption type, panels, cover ground — must read as one dark desaturated navy of the same hue on every file. The reproduced historical plates keep their own colour and are not judged. Failure: a page whose structural ink drifts to black, mid blue, warm brown or another accent hue, or a set where the navy is visibly a different colour from file to file.",
